  {
    "episode_id": 92652,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92652.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "I mean, in Congress, I think you're one of the most prominent voices in the kind of progressive wing of the Democratic Party. You know, at this time in Bay Area politics, it seems like a lot of the mayors, at least, have moved away from sort of more progressive policy positions. You got Mayor Matt Mayhand down in San Jose. You got Mayor Larry here in San Francisco. To you, what does it mean to be a progressive mayor at this moment?",
