    "turn_text": "I don't know if we need to recreate that, but I think we need to reset it. Make sure that in each neighborhood, in each council district, the appropriate structure is there for feedback and for input to the mayor. I can give you one example as a member of Congress and then formally in the state legislature, the mayor's agenda would come to me and of course I would champion the mayor's agenda. Oftentimes council members would call me and say, wait a minute, where is my priority? I don't want that If I am mayor of Oakland, I want to have the mayor's agenda to be inclusive of every single neighborhood, every single council district. And I know how this works in Sacramento and in Washington",
