    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, let me just speak to contracts for the city in general. I believe that we have to make sure that the residents of Oakland know what contracts have been negotiated, who negotiated them, for how much, what the scope of work is, are there costs overruns, And we need to strengthen our ethics commission and our close the gaps. I will not tolerate any pay to play schemes. And I am confident that if we put contracts online and distribute that information to the public, we will begin that process of transparency and accountability in contracting. Many people don't know what contracts are in the city, what they're what the amount is, what the scope of work is and who is doing that and how they were negotiated. That must become transparent so people will be able to know what the truth is about contracts and how tax payer dollars are being used for the specific purpose that the contract was issued for.",
