  {
    "episode_id": 92652,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92652.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 60,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. You know, just want to remind callers, you know, when you talk to one of the screeners, tell us what you want to ask for real. You know, we're happy to put critical questions to Barbara Lee. She's happy to take them. But, you know, don't lie to the screeners. That kind of breaks the circle of trust that the show works on. Okay. Thanks, everyone. Let's give you one of the comments here. This is something that obviously is a huge issue for Oakland voters. Brent writes, will Lee get Oakland's ruinous streets repaired? The potholes are cavernous, dangerous, and blowing out tires. If she can commit to filling potholes, I can commit my vote to her. I mean, this is, you know, bread and butter kind of local politics. Why is this so hard to get fixed? And do you think it's actually possible that a mayor can improve the puddle situation in",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_12",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Callers should truthfully state their intended question when speaking to screeners.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Barbara Lee is willing to answer important questions posed by callers.",
        "confidence": 0.95
